00,25.65],[1759276800,34.11],[1761955200,1.77],[1764547200,11.59],[1767225600,25.73],[1769904000,29.87],[1772323200,6.54],[1775001600,19.33],[1777593600,10.03],[1780272000,27.85],[1782864000,17.43],[1785542400,10.87]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does Non-POL Exports data represent?","answer":"The Non-POL Exports data represents the total value of exports from India, excluding Petroleum, Oil, and Lubricants.^This data is an important indicator of the country's export performance in sectors such as manufacturing, agriculture, textiles, and technology, other than the oil industry."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Non-POL data?","answer":"This data indicates the global demand for a country's goods and services (excluding petroleum, oil, and lubricants) and overall health of its trade relationships.^High levels of non-POL exports suggest a diversified economy not overly reliant on oil exports. It indicates the strength and global competitiveness of other sectors.^Non-POL exports contribute significantly to a country's GDP and are a key driver of economic growth.^Export levels can reflect employment rates and industrial activity, as higher exports often require increased production and labour.^Export performance can impact domestic inflation. Strong export growth can lead to increased revenue and potentially higher domestic prices, especially if it leads to a stronger domestic currency."},{"question":"How to interpret the Non-POL data?","answer":"Analyse the trends in non-POL exports over time to gauge the health and global competitiveness of various sectors in the economy.^Assess how changes in global economic conditions, such as demand in key markets and international trade policies, affect non-POL exports.^Evaluate the impact of export performance on the domestic economy, including GDP growth, industrial activity, and employment.^Consider the influence of exchange rate fluctuations on export competitiveness and its subsequent impact on export levels.^Analyse the role of government policies, trade agreements, and infrastructure development in supporting or hindering non-POL exports."}],"related":[{"slug":"baltic-dry-index","title":"Baltic Dry Index"},{"slug":"crude-oil-price-indian-basket","title":"Crude Oil Price (Indian Basket)"},{"slug":"external-commercial-borrowings-ecbs","title":"External Commercial Borrowings (ECBs)"},{"slug":"foreign-exchange-reserves","title":"Foreign Exchange Reserves"},{"slug":"foreign-tourist-arrivals","title":"Foreign Tourist Arrivals"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-direct-investment-fdi","title":"Gross Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-portfolio-investment-fpi","title":"Gross Foreign Portfolio Investment (FPI)"},{"slug":"import-cover-months","title":"Import Cover (Months)"},{"slug":"international-air-passenger-traffic","title":"Air Passenger Traffic - International"},{"slug":"port-cargo-traffic","title":"Port Cargo Traffic"},{"slug":"services-trade-net-inflows","title":"Services Trade- Net Inflows"}],"title":"Non-Oil Exports","description":"India's non-oil exports stand at $ 53,985.2 Million for Aug 2026. Stripping out oil gives a cleaner read on underlying external demand.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's non-oil exports stand at $ 53,985.2 Million for Aug 2026. Stripping out oil gives a cleaner read on underlying external demand.","Y-o-Y":"India's non-oil exports stand at 10.87% for Aug 2026. Stripping out oil gives a cleaner read on underlying external demand."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-08-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-13T15:27:59+00:00"}